I've read the files and haven't edited anything. Here's the plan.

**How login starts a session** (`src/api/routes.ts:8-13`): `authenticate`, then `createSession(user.id)`, then it returns `{ token: session.token }`. Signup will do the same `createSession(user.id)` call.

I'll call `createSession` directly instead of importing `login` from `routes.ts`. `routes.ts` already imports `accountRoutes` from `account.ts`, so going the other way would create a circular import. Calling `login` would also run a second scrypt password check for no benefit.

Another agent may change how login starts a session before I edit. If they do, I'll copy whatever login does at that point.

### 1. `src/api/account.ts`
Change the two imports:
```ts
import { createUser, getUser, publicUser, UserError } from "../auth/users.ts";
import { createSession, revokeSession } from "../auth/session.ts";
```
Add this entry to the end of `accountRoutes`, after `/api/logout`:
```ts
  {
    method: "POST",
    path: "/api/signup",
    handler: (req) => {
      const email = field(req.body, "email");
      const password = field(req.body, "password");
      if (!email || !password) return json(400, { error: "email and password are required" });
      try {
        const user = createUser(email, field(req.body, "name") ?? "", password);
        const session = createSession(user.id);
        return json(201, { token: session.token, user: publicUser(user) });
      } catch (err) {
        if (err instanceof UserError) return json(400, { error: err.message });
        throw err;
      }
    },
  },
```
- **Missing fields:** if email or password is missing, signup returns 400, the same as login. If I passed `undefined` through instead, `createUser` would crash on `.trim()` and the router would return a 500.
- **Name is optional:** `createUser` already uses the email as the name when the name is blank.
- **Other errors:** anything that isn't a `UserError` is rethrown, so the router still returns 500 for it.

### 2. `test/signup.test.ts` (new)
```ts
import { test, beforeEach } from "node:test";
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { app } from "../src/api/routes.ts";
import { resetUsers } from "../src/auth/users.ts";
import { resetSessions } from "../src/auth/session.ts";

const call = (method: string, path: string, body?: unknown, token?: string) =>
  app({ method, path, body, headers: token ? { authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } : {} });

beforeEach(() => {
  resetUsers();
  resetSessions();
});

test("signup creates the user and returns a working session token", async () => {
  const res = await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "Grace@Example.com", name: "Grace", password: "hopper1906" });
  assert.equal(res.status, 201);
  const { token, user } = res.body as { token: string; user: { id: string; email: string; name: string } };
  assert.deepEqual(user, { id: user.id, email: "grace@example.com", name: "Grace" });
  assert.ok(!("passwordHash" in user));
  const me = await call("GET", "/api/me", undefined, token);
  assert.equal(me.status, 200);
  assert.deepEqual(me.body, user);
});

test("signed-up user can log in with the same password", async () => {
  await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "grace@example.com", name: "Grace", password: "hopper1906" });
  assert.equal((await call("POST", "/api/login", { email: "grace@example.com", password: "hopper1906" })).status, 200);
});

test("signup maps UserError to 400", async () => {
  await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "grace@example.com", name: "Grace", password: "hopper1906" });
  const dup = await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "GRACE@example.com", name: "G", password: "another-pass" });
  assert.deepEqual(dup, { status: 400, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: { error: "email already registered" } });
  assert.deepEqual((await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "nope", password: "hopper1906" })).body, { error: "invalid email" });
  assert.deepEqual((await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "x@y.z", password: "short" })).body, { error: "password must be at least 8 characters" });
});

test("signup requires email and password", async () => {
  assert.equal((await call("POST", "/api/signup", { email: "grace@example.com" })).status, 400);
  assert.equal((await call("POST", "/api/signup", {})).status, 400);
});
```

